  "slug": "prediction-antimicrobial-peptide-e8c1",
  "summary": "Recent preprints test protein and RNA predictors against curated annotations, chemical probing data and conformational ensembles.",
  "synthesis": "Across these preprints, the common thread is whether predictor outputs are checked against independent biological reference data. The interpretability study tests ESMC probe, neuron and layer conclusions against residue-level curated annotations and reports that these conclusions depend on the method applied. MXfold2 is extended to learn RNA secondary structure from chemical probing data using implicit maximum-likelihood training. MANTA separates geometric prior estimation from coordinate generation for intrinsically disordered protein ensembles and identifies prior estimation as the main bottleneck. DynamicsPLM adds molecular dynamics heads to a 35M-parameter protein language model for zero-shot mutation effect prediction. Region-aware pooling of mRNA foundation model embeddings improves linear probe performance over global mean pooling. FoldMapper and A2Holo extend structure-based design and apo-to-holo conformational transition prediction. The new element is less a single method than a shift toward validating representations and predictions against curated, experimental or dynamical references.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
